WEBVTT

00:13.938 --> 00:14.772
Oh, well...

00:27.326 --> 00:28.703
Wait-- What's going on?

00:29.287 --> 00:32.331
Seriously, don't just barge in like that!

00:32.415 --> 00:33.583
Sorry!

00:35.877 --> 00:38.171
Why do I have to apologize?

00:38.254 --> 00:40.339
You'll be in trouble if you catch a cold!

00:40.923 --> 00:43.176
That's a whole different story!

00:43.259 --> 00:45.553
"We won't invade each other's territory."

00:45.636 --> 00:47.680
We agreed when we got to 6th grade, right?

00:50.057 --> 00:51.684
What the heck?

00:53.895 --> 00:55.229
Hey, Yu.

00:55.313 --> 00:56.355
What is it?

00:57.064 --> 00:58.941
Thanks for the blanket.

02:32.285 --> 02:33.953
DEVILS' CREST

02:34.036 --> 02:37.915
EPISODE 3: AWAKENING

02:41.919 --> 02:45.965
I'm sure everyone from Class 1
is barricaded inside.

02:46.048 --> 02:47.425
We have to do something.

02:49.427 --> 02:50.803
That won't work.

02:50.887 --> 02:54.098
That guy probably has really high HP
and physical defense.

02:54.181 --> 02:55.683
But we can't just leave it.

02:56.434 --> 02:57.768
I know.

02:57.852 --> 02:59.854
We have to fight using magic,

02:59.937 --> 03:02.857
but my MP hasn't even
recovered to half yet.

03:03.524 --> 03:06.444
<i>Think. How can we beat it?</i>

03:06.986 --> 03:09.155
<i>Even if the system works like in the game,</i>

03:09.238 --> 03:11.407
<i>there are no weapon or item shops here.</i>

03:12.283 --> 03:15.286
<i>This is reality. Actual reality.</i>

03:21.042 --> 03:23.544
Sawa, Konken, can you guys escape...

03:23.628 --> 03:26.339
No, wait, can you run around it
for just a minute?

03:28.674 --> 03:29.508
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

03:29.592 --> 03:31.177
But what are you planning?

03:31.260 --> 03:32.511
Let me handle it for now.

03:40.186 --> 03:41.479
I'll grab aggro.

03:41.562 --> 03:43.481
Cover me from the side.

03:43.564 --> 03:44.440
Got it!

03:45.942 --> 03:47.568
Over here, monster!

03:49.362 --> 03:50.529
Over here, over here!

03:50.613 --> 03:52.114
Hey, what are you looking at?

03:55.284 --> 03:56.118
Go!

03:58.245 --> 03:59.121
Hey!

04:02.500 --> 04:05.878
<i>Sawa, Konken, hang in there!</i>

04:06.796 --> 04:07.755
DOCTOR'S OFFICE

04:15.721 --> 04:16.973
This should be enough.

04:18.975 --> 04:21.143
Hey, demon, over here.

04:21.727 --> 04:22.603
Come on, come on!

04:35.199 --> 04:36.158
Take this!

04:36.993 --> 04:38.244
Durendal!

04:44.959 --> 04:45.918
Ouch.

04:54.677 --> 04:55.553
Yu!

04:58.139 --> 04:59.932
Yu, what was that?

05:00.016 --> 05:01.559
Ethanol for disinfection.

05:01.642 --> 05:04.437
I see. So, it's a substitute for magic.

05:04.520 --> 05:05.563
Yeah.

05:05.646 --> 05:07.940
But how will you light it?

05:09.442 --> 05:10.443
Well...

05:10.526 --> 05:12.945
You didn't even think that far?

05:13.029 --> 05:13.904
YUMA ASHIHARA
ALTEA

05:13.988 --> 05:15.573
If I run for another minute,

05:15.656 --> 05:19.243
I should have enough MP restored
to cast one Flame Arrow.

05:26.709 --> 05:29.503
Wait, let me try something first.

05:30.463 --> 05:31.380
Try what?

05:38.137 --> 05:38.971
Now!

05:45.728 --> 05:49.899
CONEHEAD BRUISER

05:49.982 --> 05:52.777
Wow, it's really working!

05:52.860 --> 05:55.821
But it's taking longer to run out
than I thought.

05:56.363 --> 05:58.866
It's just that there's a lot of HP.

06:05.748 --> 06:08.167
CONEHEAD BRUISER

06:09.335 --> 06:13.631
For a monster, this thing
is just like a real living creature...

06:14.757 --> 06:17.176
These aren't just 3D objects.

06:17.885 --> 06:20.679
But that's probably only
while they're alive.

06:22.014 --> 06:23.474
What do you mean?

06:33.776 --> 06:35.277
You're kidding!

06:35.361 --> 06:36.695
No way.

06:37.404 --> 06:39.865
With that much left,
a physical attack should...

06:40.533 --> 06:43.494
No, wait, I need to refill
with fresh ethanol.

06:49.166 --> 06:50.084
Yu!

06:50.167 --> 06:51.585
Yuumy!

06:52.962 --> 06:54.213
Let me go!

07:01.929 --> 07:02.805
Yu!

07:03.430 --> 07:04.682
Stop it!

07:13.524 --> 07:15.151
Get away now, Yu!

07:19.113 --> 07:19.947
Let him go!

07:20.030 --> 07:22.324
Don't give up, Yuumy!

07:25.911 --> 07:27.580
YUMA ASHIHARA

07:48.434 --> 07:49.602
Where am I?

07:53.856 --> 07:56.734
The stars are... falling.

07:58.027 --> 07:58.944
That's right.

08:00.321 --> 08:03.365
That's what you call the P-T Boundary.

08:04.033 --> 08:08.120
It's the very thing that triggered the
largest mass extinction in Earth's history

08:08.204 --> 08:10.331
at the end of the Permian period.

08:11.749 --> 08:17.254
Soon, 95% of all life on this planet
will be wiped out.

08:17.755 --> 08:19.798
Oh, no! We've got to do something!

08:21.300 --> 08:22.885
Unfortunately, there's no way.

08:24.094 --> 08:28.390
At this point,
neither angels nor devils can stop it.

08:28.474 --> 08:31.143
Angels? Devils?

08:31.727 --> 08:36.982
Besides, this happened
250 million years ago.

08:38.359 --> 08:40.444
If it weren't for that mass extinction,

08:41.028 --> 08:45.241
you modern humans wouldn't exist, Yuma.

08:45.741 --> 08:48.285
Who are you?

08:49.370 --> 08:51.580
Should you really be
worrying about that now?

08:52.164 --> 08:55.042
You're on the verge of death right now.

08:56.752 --> 08:59.338
Am I dead?

08:59.838 --> 09:02.007
The thread of life is still connected.

09:03.634 --> 09:07.137
But how on earth
could I have survived that?

09:07.221 --> 09:09.598
Adjust the angle of the rod

09:10.307 --> 09:12.768
and use the Monster Tamer's power.

09:14.061 --> 09:15.521
At the same time.

09:16.105 --> 09:17.690
How do you know all this?

09:18.983 --> 09:20.401
It doesn't matter right now.

09:21.026 --> 09:24.029
Do you want to live?
Or will you accept death?

09:25.030 --> 09:28.909
That monster is going to kill
your friend and your sister, too.

09:32.079 --> 09:34.415
Okay. I'll do it.

09:34.498 --> 09:35.582
Good.

09:36.083 --> 09:38.168
I bet on you, after all.

09:39.378 --> 09:41.213
Now, wake up.

09:42.047 --> 09:45.217
Three, two, one...

09:58.439 --> 09:59.481
Aperta!

10:28.635 --> 10:30.304
CONEHEAD BRUISER

10:37.144 --> 10:38.187
Yuumy!

10:39.146 --> 10:40.272
I'm fine.

11:01.168 --> 11:02.336
Sumika!

11:02.419 --> 11:03.462
Watamaki...

11:04.171 --> 11:06.548
Watamaki is my familiar.

11:07.424 --> 11:11.887
At the very least,
she shouldn't see us as targets.

11:15.599 --> 11:16.892
Yuumy!

11:26.110 --> 11:30.531
I'm... coming...

11:31.156 --> 11:32.157
<i>I knew it.</i>

11:32.241 --> 11:35.869
<i>Deep down somewhere,
the real Watamaki is there.</i>

11:46.004 --> 11:47.631
Thank you, Watamaki.

11:48.173 --> 11:50.217
I promise to bring you back to yourself.

11:52.386 --> 11:53.512
Clause.

12:06.066 --> 12:08.527
ALTEA 1F

12:08.610 --> 12:10.904
But this is the real world...

12:11.447 --> 12:13.365
All right, we leveled up!

12:14.241 --> 12:16.869
Yu, you leveled up too, right?

12:16.952 --> 12:19.455
So, does that mean
if we land even a single hit,

12:19.538 --> 12:21.790
we split the experience point evenly?

12:21.874 --> 12:23.834
It's the same as Actual Magic.

12:25.002 --> 12:25.878
BRUISING HAMMER

12:25.961 --> 12:29.423
The Item Drop log is shown
along with the Level Up log.

12:29.506 --> 12:31.800
The drop? Seriously?

12:32.342 --> 12:34.428
If it's the same as Actual Magic,

12:34.511 --> 12:36.013
it should be in the inventory.

12:36.096 --> 12:37.306
TEST PASS CERTIFICATE CARD

12:37.931 --> 12:41.351
I see. So, we have an inventory
in this world too, huh?

12:42.019 --> 12:43.520
It was very powerful.

12:43.604 --> 12:46.148
I bet you got a pretty good item,
didn't you?

12:46.231 --> 12:48.317
The test pass certificate card...

12:48.400 --> 12:50.819
A card you got at the playtest, huh?

12:50.903 --> 12:53.071
Monster card, Squeak!

12:54.323 --> 12:56.450
Squeak? That one?

12:56.533 --> 13:00.037
The weapons and armor I got
during the playtest are gone,

13:00.120 --> 13:01.455
so why do I have Squeak?

13:01.538 --> 13:03.457
Hey, isn't this a potion?

13:05.542 --> 13:07.211
LESSER HP POTION

13:10.756 --> 13:12.216
Lesser potions, really?

13:12.299 --> 13:14.426
Even lesser potions are precious.

13:15.177 --> 13:17.721
Unlike real-world medicine or bandages,

13:17.804 --> 13:20.140
it heals you instantly
the moment you drink it.

13:20.807 --> 13:22.017
Probably.

13:22.100 --> 13:23.477
Well, I guess so.

13:23.560 --> 13:24.561
Thanks.

13:29.316 --> 13:31.068
Okay, I got it.

13:31.151 --> 13:32.069
Me too.

13:33.820 --> 13:34.905
If we go outside,

13:34.988 --> 13:38.992
we might be able to ask the police
or the fire department for help.

13:39.076 --> 13:41.745
But the automatic doors won't open, right?

13:41.828 --> 13:43.497
Konken, use this.

13:43.580 --> 13:44.498
BRUISING HAMMER

13:45.999 --> 13:48.001
You got a weapon too?

13:48.585 --> 13:50.837
All right, leave this to me!

13:57.094 --> 13:58.762
Hey, are you okay?

14:00.889 --> 14:02.516
What the heck is this?

14:03.100 --> 14:05.852
I guess it's protected
by some kind of magic.

14:06.478 --> 14:10.482
I don't think there's anything we can do
to break this glass right now.

14:10.566 --> 14:11.483
Magic?

14:12.401 --> 14:13.485
The other glass too.

14:14.111 --> 14:17.155
No, every wall and door
is probably the same.

14:18.115 --> 14:21.535
So, we're completely trapped, huh?

14:21.618 --> 14:23.787
Can't we get out of Altea?

14:32.629 --> 14:34.047
It'll be okay.

14:34.131 --> 14:38.176
If it's magic, there must be a way
to dispel it, right?

14:38.802 --> 14:40.262
First, let's find Nagi

14:40.345 --> 14:42.306
and get Watamaki back to herself.

14:44.266 --> 14:45.309
Yu...

14:46.310 --> 14:47.894
Of course, we will!

14:47.978 --> 14:50.856
Let's get our party of four
back together ASAP!

14:55.527 --> 14:57.237
Guess we'll head back, then.

14:57.321 --> 15:00.699
We've got to tell the guys in Class 1
that it's safe now.

15:00.782 --> 15:02.534
Wait, before we do that,

15:03.201 --> 15:05.912
let's just form a party
with us three for now.

15:06.455 --> 15:08.498
We can see each other's HP,

15:08.582 --> 15:11.209
and we'll get experience points
even if we don't fight.

15:11.293 --> 15:12.169
FRIEND REQUEST

15:14.379 --> 15:15.380
WILL YOU JOIN?

15:15.464 --> 15:16.298
You bet!

15:16.381 --> 15:18.759
If the monster shows up again,

15:18.842 --> 15:22.179
I'm gonna knock it out cold
with my physical power.

15:26.600 --> 15:28.310
SAWA ASHIHARA

15:29.770 --> 15:30.771
ALTEA 1F

15:30.854 --> 15:31.688
What is it?

15:32.230 --> 15:34.066
Well, never mind.

15:34.149 --> 15:35.275
Hey, Yu.

15:35.984 --> 15:37.194
What is it?

15:37.277 --> 15:40.322
Where did you find
that ethanol from earlier?

15:41.573 --> 15:42.741
In the back room.

15:43.909 --> 15:44.951
I see.

15:45.661 --> 15:48.330
Konken, will you go ahead
to where everyone is?

15:49.539 --> 15:51.583
What about you two?

15:51.667 --> 15:54.169
I'm dressed like this, you know?

15:54.252 --> 15:55.962
I want to find something to wear.

15:58.715 --> 15:59.841
That's true.

15:59.925 --> 16:01.468
Then I'll go ahead.

16:02.678 --> 16:03.553
Please.

16:10.644 --> 16:13.480
Weren't you supposed
to be looking for your clothes?

16:13.563 --> 16:14.981
Why are we in the infirmary?

16:15.565 --> 16:16.733
Show me.

16:21.279 --> 16:23.907
That's a relief. It's a shallow cut.

16:24.533 --> 16:26.159
I'll disinfect it just in case.

16:29.955 --> 16:33.375
TEST PASS CERTIFICATE CARD
MONSTER CARD - SQUEAK

16:33.458 --> 16:35.377
DISINFECTANT

16:35.961 --> 16:37.212
I knew it!

16:37.295 --> 16:40.424
Looks like you can store
real-world items in the storage too.

16:41.550 --> 16:44.761
Yu, open your storage
and put everything here in there.

16:46.179 --> 16:47.139
Okay.

16:57.190 --> 16:58.859
- Break the glass?
- Yes.

16:59.526 --> 17:02.154
No way. Even if it is an emergency...

17:02.946 --> 17:04.740
Yu, calm down and listen.

17:05.407 --> 17:08.410
I don't think we'll be able
to get out of here for a while.

17:08.493 --> 17:09.953
How long?

17:10.036 --> 17:12.164
Two or three days, maybe ten,

17:12.247 --> 17:13.582
or possibly even longer.

17:15.417 --> 17:18.628
Come on, it can't be that long.

17:19.129 --> 17:21.923
There must be a huge commotion
outside by now.

17:23.759 --> 17:26.928
If we used a bulldozer or something,
even that glass would surely...

17:27.012 --> 17:28.680
You already know, right?

17:28.764 --> 17:30.265
Altea is currently

17:30.348 --> 17:33.518
being gradually overtaken
by the world of Actual Magic.

17:35.645 --> 17:37.564
What if the glass were reinforced

17:37.647 --> 17:40.650
with some kind of top-tier magic
powerful enough to stop a meteorite?

17:41.234 --> 17:43.361
Do you think a bulldozer could smash that?

17:45.489 --> 17:47.866
Anyway, I'm not stockpiling just for now.

17:48.366 --> 17:52.579
A safe shelter, food, water, and medicine,

17:53.079 --> 17:55.040
those are going to be really important.

17:55.874 --> 17:57.793
There'll definitely be trouble eventually.

17:58.376 --> 18:00.504
Are you trying to hog it all
for ourselves?

18:00.587 --> 18:01.797
No!

18:01.880 --> 18:04.758
I'm securing it
before someone else grabs it

18:04.841 --> 18:06.718
and making sure it's shared fairly.

18:06.802 --> 18:08.512
Then it doesn't have to be now--

18:08.595 --> 18:10.680
I don't want to regret it
when it's too late!

18:15.393 --> 18:18.271
Besides, if we have medicine and food,

18:18.355 --> 18:21.691
we'll be in a better position
if we have to negotiate with someone.

18:28.323 --> 18:31.743
Are you... really Sawa?

18:32.410 --> 18:33.870
What?

18:34.955 --> 18:36.623
Okay, I get it.

18:36.706 --> 18:39.251
Let's put as much as we can
into the storage.

18:41.545 --> 18:44.548
I can't get the stuff inside
without breaking the glass.

18:44.631 --> 18:48.385
But I really don't want the food
to get covered in glass shards.

18:49.135 --> 18:51.012
Then why don't we experiment?

18:51.638 --> 18:52.514
Experiment?

18:55.392 --> 18:57.519
I'll try putting this into storage.

19:08.864 --> 19:11.783
Wow! The dirt came off!

19:11.867 --> 19:14.494
Yeah. I was thinking
that anything other than items

19:14.578 --> 19:17.414
might not be allowed by the system.

19:17.497 --> 19:20.417
I see. Good thinking, Yu!

19:26.798 --> 19:30.093
At least we're all set for water, food,
and medicine for now.

19:30.927 --> 19:33.054
Thanks for your help, Yu.

19:34.556 --> 19:36.683
Could you stick around a little longer?

19:40.020 --> 19:41.438
WOMEN'S LOCKER ROOM

19:41.521 --> 19:43.440
Well, it's pretty big.

19:46.067 --> 19:48.945
But that's actually a good thing.
I can hide my wings in it.

19:49.779 --> 19:51.114
Let's go back to the lobby--

19:51.197 --> 19:52.699
Wait, hold up, Sawa!

19:54.242 --> 19:58.455
Konken and I just got a bigger QREST,

19:58.538 --> 20:00.999
but for only you
to grow something like that...

20:01.082 --> 20:02.918
It just doesn't make any sense!

20:05.253 --> 20:06.421
Can you come over?

20:13.011 --> 20:15.305
Hey, where did you get that?

20:15.388 --> 20:16.848
Inside the locker.

20:16.932 --> 20:18.516
But look closely.

20:23.188 --> 20:25.440
My hair is blue!

20:26.232 --> 20:27.651
It's not just me.

20:28.234 --> 20:31.279
To varying degrees,
your body is changing too.

20:31.947 --> 20:34.574
Probably Konken
and everyone else in the class as well.

20:37.160 --> 20:39.162
I feel a lump...

20:40.830 --> 20:42.082
What is this?

20:43.375 --> 20:46.753
Could we be going through the same thing
that happened to Watamaki?

20:47.295 --> 20:49.464
Will we end up like that someday too?

20:50.256 --> 20:53.259
<i>I don't think we'll end up like Sumika.</i>

20:53.969 --> 20:56.471
<i>Her transformation
was kind of an exception.</i>

20:59.391 --> 21:00.642
Hey, Sawa,

21:00.725 --> 21:04.062
you know something
you haven't told me yet, don't you?

21:04.646 --> 21:08.149
What's happening to us, to Altea?

21:13.363 --> 21:14.239
Please,

21:14.990 --> 21:16.908
just give me a little more time.

21:19.327 --> 21:22.998
Once things calm down,
I'll tell you everything I know.

21:25.458 --> 21:26.668
But right now,

21:26.751 --> 21:29.170
I want to look into it more
and think it over.

21:30.213 --> 21:31.131
So...

21:33.800 --> 21:35.176
Yeah, I get it.

21:36.428 --> 21:39.180
Sorry for making it sound like
I don't trust you.

21:39.848 --> 21:42.934
I know you're doing your best.

21:49.441 --> 21:51.443
Cut the crap!

21:52.277 --> 21:55.196
I bet you're a monster too!

21:55.280 --> 21:56.489
Kondo!

23:28.039 --> 23:28.915
SUSPICION

23:28.998 --> 23:30.959
<i>- What are you saying, Gamo?
- Where's Watamaki?</i>

23:31.042 --> 23:32.085
<i>What makes us monsters?</i>

23:32.168 --> 23:33.128
<i>You didn't kill her...</i>

23:33.211 --> 23:35.672
<i>That was magic, right?</i>

23:36.172 --> 23:37.298
<i>Mo-yan?</i>

23:37.382 --> 23:39.926
<i>Tomochi protected me,</i>

23:40.718 --> 23:42.971
<i>but I left her behind...</i>

23:43.054 --> 23:45.056
Translated by Kanako Murakoshi
